  23. Mixed-Tip Response Attack

  Attack: can a production code path produce indexed_height/hash from tip N and monetary values from tip N+1 (or vice versa) in a single response?

  Answer: No. Both reads (statusFrom and supplyRollupValuesFrom) run against the same pgx.Tx opened at REPEATABLE READ isolation before either read executes. PostgreSQL guarantees every statement in that transaction sees a snapshot fixed at the transaction's start time. A concurrent ApplyBlock committing between the two statements does not affect what the in-flight transaction observes. Even if the transaction were not used, block_supply_rollup rows are immutable — the row named by the captured anchor hash cannot change after the anchor is captured. No production path can produce a mixed-tip response. PASS.

